1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[Netero] Do not underestimate
humans, Meruem.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
[Meruem] What is this?

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
[Netero] Meruem, King of the Ants,

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
within the human heart.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
[tense music playing]

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
From the very beginning,
checkmate was yours.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
[opening theme music playing]

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[singer singing in English]

10
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
[singer singing in English]

12
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:44,000
but despite this, it also
proved surprisingly lethal.

14
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
to mass-produce these bombs
in short time,

15
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
making it a favorite among dictatorships.

16
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
This, along with the peculiar shape
of the fallout cloud,

17
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
earned this bomb the name
"Miniature Rose,"

18
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
or the "Poor Man's Rose."

19
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
which effectively banned
the bomb's production.

20
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
[imperceptible]

21
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
However, over 80% of countries

22
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
rejected the proposal
to discard the existing Roses

23
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
that had already been produced.

24
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
This means that even today
in far too many countries,

25
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
hundreds upon thousands of seeds

26
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
still wait silently
for their chance to bloom.

27
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
"Were humans really
so different from Ants?"

28
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
-[bomb explodes]
-[both gasp]

29
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
[narrator] A plume of smoke
rose in the distance,

30
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
At the same time, outside of the palace,

31
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Pouf's segment found itself
looking Knuckle in the eye.

32
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[gasps]

33
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
[narrator] After his experience
with Youpi,

34
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Knuckle hoped that he would be able

35
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
to reach a similar understanding
with Pouf,

36
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
but his hopes, faint as they were,

37
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
were utterly shattered.

38
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[sighs]

39
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
The King can just wave his hand

40
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
and turn all of them into evil spawn.

41
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
[Knuckle] I see.

42
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Pouf's real body must have learned

43
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
that something happened to the King.

44
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Then the segment's face transformed,

45
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
revealing its true nature.

46
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Did the Chairman defeat the King?

47
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Well, I suppose
it doesn't matter either way.

48
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[narrator] When he looked
at Pouf's face,

49
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Is everyone okay?

50
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[grunting]

51
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[gasps]

52
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[wind blowing]

53
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
This is brutal.

54
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
It only took them 30 minutes
to wreck the whole place.

55
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
That was close.

56
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
-[Killua] Ikalgo.
-[gasps]

57
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
[gasps] Killua!

58
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[dramatic music playing]

59
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
It's Palm.

60
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
I see. I'm glad you're here.

61
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
You finally made it back to us.

62
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Now do you remember the plan?

63
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
I'll take you to the capital by car.

64
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
No. It turns out she wants to stay.

65
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Well, she ought to be pretty useful
in a fight at least.

66
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[Gon] I'll wait right here for one hour.

67
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
[Killua] And once he's made up his mind,

68
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
he won't budge.

69
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:21,000
But to be honest,
that situation is ideal.

70
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
is try to stay out of his way.

71
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Well, sure, but what if he--

72
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Yeah. Yeah, I know.

73
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,000
If Gon's in trouble,
we'll all rush in to help him out.

74
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Let's just be ready
for whatever happens with him.

75
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
[Ikalgo] Oh, I get it.
So that's what staying means, huh?

76
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Even if Gon uses all the power
he has right now,

77
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
it won't be enough.

78
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
He still won't be able to beat Pitou.

79
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
In fact, even if all three of us join him,

80
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Pitou still has us outmatched

81
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
and knows that just as well as we do.

82
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Killua] Okay. Let's go.

83
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
[Knuckle] We separated the King
and the Royal Guards

84
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Do we stop or keep going?

85
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
[tense music playing]

86
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
You're done, right?

87
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
[Neferpitou gasps]

88
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[Neferpitou] Why did he say that?

89
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
I may have relaxed a bit,

90
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
and if he noticed,

91
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
then in that instant…

92
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
I have to kill him.

93
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
No matter the cost.

94
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,000
I must… for the King's sake.

95
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Did he sense my bloodlust then?

96
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
It's time for us to go to Peijing.

97
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
It'll be a lot faster if we run there.

98
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
[Komugi whimpering]

99
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
What happened to me?

100
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Komugi] I… I'm sorry!

101
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
I'm so rude. Am I interrupting?

102
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
[narrator] Pitou was close enough
to decapitate Gon with one arm,

103
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
[gasps]

104
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Oh, and if Pitou tries to run away,

105
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[Neferpitou gasps]

106
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[whimpering]

107
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
[Gon] Thanks a lot, Knuckle,

108
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
but it's okay.

109
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
For some reason, I trust Pitou.

110
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
[gasps]

111
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
So do me a favor, Knuckle.

112
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Take care of that girl for us
until we see Kite.

113
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
[gasps]

114
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Uh, are you guys talking about me?

115
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
[dramatic music playing]

116
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
[gasps]

117
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[Neferpitou] Does he seriously plan to…

118
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
[Knuckle] Use the girl as a hostage?

119
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
I promise you that.

120
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
So I guess that means, for now,

121
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
you're just gonna have to trust me too.

122
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Right, Pitou?

123
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
[whimpers]

124
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
It's fine. Leave the rest to Pitou and me.

125
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:08,000
It's okay. That was always
the plan, wasn't it?

126
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Truth is, I feel better
after hearing what he's doing.

127
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
How many bloodbaths
did they have to endure

128
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
to start thinking like that?

129
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Uh…

130
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,000
[Palm] It's all right.

131
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Now that I've laid my eyes on Gon,

132
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
if something happens,
I'll know about it immediately.

133
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
[Killua] Besides it's not like Pitou
is gonna abandon her,

134
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
which means that Gon is safe for now.

135
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
[all sigh]

136
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
[Komugi] What's happening?

137
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,000
I don't understand what's going on here.

138
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[fire crackling]

139
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
that it melted the rock into magma,

140
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,000
leaving a scene resembling
the mouth of an active volcano,

141
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:42,000
a perpetual cloud of black smoke
driving all life away.

142
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
[Shaiapouf gasping]

143
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Hey, Pouf!

144
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[gasps]

145
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
It's possible the explosion
may have sent the King flying.

146
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
You know, I was wrong.

147
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
We'll kill every one of them…

148
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
by the King's side.

149
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Not a single one will be spared.

150
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
[gasping]

151
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
[tense music playing]

152
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
[gasps]

153
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
[groans]

154
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
[gasps]

155
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[imperceptible]

156
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:07,000
[narrator] Youpi's howl was not a sign
of good things to come,

157
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,000
and before he even realized it himself,

158
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
[imperceptible]

159
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[suspenseful music playing]

160
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
[closing theme music playing]

161
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[upbeat music playing]

162
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, "Unparalleled Joy
and Unconditional Love."

163
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Killua] Yeah, I never ask
for anything in return.

164
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Gon] That's unconditional love.

165
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
[Killua] Unparalleled joy.
